WEBVTT

00:00:09.170 --> 00:00:09.990
Ugh.

00:00:13.310 --> 00:00:16.240
Seeing you first thing in 
the morning spoils my mood.

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:19.030
I could say the same to you.

00:00:22.550 --> 00:00:23.500
It's her...

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:26.500
I can't believe that morning run.

00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:30.590
She's a fitness junkie. 
She reminds me of you.

00:00:31.350 --> 00:00:33.720
I exercise for work reasons.

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:35.560
It's different from her hobby.

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:36.890
"Hobby"?

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:39.850
Would someone go that hard for a hobby?

00:00:42.810 --> 00:00:44.340
She lives alone, you know.

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:45.020
Huh?

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:47.220
Uchida-san told me.

00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:50.880
She came alone to Tokyo so 
she could compete in track,

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:53.070
and the job is for living expenses.

00:00:55.420 --> 00:00:59.160
I know how you are about girls, 
so why are you okay with her?

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:03.660
I guess 'cause she's not girly.

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:04.850
Fair enough.

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:07.330
Is that all?

00:01:07.330 --> 00:01:08.950
Piss off!

00:01:08.950 --> 00:01:12.120
I don't see you even trying to hide 
your crap personality from her.

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:16.010
There's no point in making nice with someone

00:01:16.010 --> 00:01:18.030
who didn't even know we were pop idols.

00:01:18.030 --> 00:01:20.260
Crap personality is right...

00:01:22.970 --> 00:01:26.480
<i>I'm charmed by how you go all-out</i>

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:30.980
<i>I'm charmed by your supportive smile</i>

00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:35.360
<i>"I must kiss you," says your Romeo</i>

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:39.320
<i>Glad that you exist and that he met you</i>

00:01:40.010 --> 00:01:43.560
<b>Heroines Run the Show</b>

00:01:47.210 --> 00:01:50.960
<i>I need more love, want to see you again soon</i>

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:55.050
<i>Lock eyes with you and tell you</i>

00:01:55.050 --> 00:01:58.970
<i>My sincerest "Thank you for everything"</i>

00:01:58.970 --> 00:02:02.970
<i>Will you love me—
not as a fan, but for real?</i>

00:02:02.970 --> 00:02:06.200
<i>"Pick me"</i>

00:02:06.910 --> 00:02:09.980
<i>"No, pick me"</i>

00:02:10.850 --> 00:02:14.860
<i>Choose which kiss you want</i>

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:17.980
<i>And let your Romeo bind you</i>

00:02:18.950 --> 00:02:22.420
<i>I'm charmed by how you go all-out</i>

00:02:22.420 --> 00:02:27.040
<i>I'm charmed watching you sing with me</i>

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:30.330
<i>I'm even charmed by your tears</i>

00:02:30.330 --> 00:02:34.690
<i>I'm charmed by your supportive smile</i>

00:02:34.690 --> 00:02:38.130
<i>Thank you for coming to meet me</i>

00:02:38.130 --> 00:02:42.610
<i>Thank you for calling my name</i>

00:02:42.610 --> 00:02:47.010
<i>"I must kiss you," says your Romeo</i>

00:02:47.010 --> 00:02:51.350
<i>Glad that you exist and that he met you</i>

00:02:57.480 --> 00:02:59.650
Hiyori-chan, that's a new personal best!

00:03:00.070 --> 00:03:01.530
Really?!

00:03:04.900 --> 00:03:06.740
Yay!

00:03:09.830 --> 00:03:13.590
"Oh, no! My first-year might 
leave me in the dust!"

00:03:13.590 --> 00:03:16.380
Quit giving me weird voiceovers, Kotaro.

00:03:16.760 --> 00:03:18.340
Was I right?

00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:21.010
No! I was thinking, 
"I'd better work hard, too!"

00:03:22.690 --> 00:03:25.010
<i>My goal is to run at nationals.</i>

00:03:26.190 --> 00:03:30.140
<i>My dream might come true pretty soon!</i>

00:03:30.140 --> 00:03:31.890
<b>Guidance Office</b>

00:03:30.650 --> 00:03:33.350
What do you mean, "can't compete"?

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:36.080
It's a school rule.

00:03:36.430 --> 00:03:40.020
Anyone with a failing grade on their 
most recent midterms or final exams

00:03:40.020 --> 00:03:43.240
is barred from athletic competitions.

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:45.970
Were the midterms difficult for you?

00:03:45.970 --> 00:03:47.840
It's more, well...

00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:52.250
I'm sorry. I couldn't 
find much time to study.

00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:55.570
I know you're busy,

00:03:55.570 --> 00:03:58.250
but if you don't score better on your finals,

00:03:58.250 --> 00:03:59.930
it'll be a bit of a problem.

00:04:01.610 --> 00:04:06.970
<i>Forget "a bit." This is a </i>huge<i> problem!</i>

00:04:07.650 --> 00:04:11.960
<i>I was so sure I'd clear any obstacle...</i>

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:14.200
<i>But now I'm facin'</i>

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:16.650
<b>Final Exams</b>

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:16.650
<i>the biggest one of all...
the hurdle known as "final exams"!</i>

00:04:17.080 --> 00:04:17.940
<i>If I don't do somethin',</i>

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:20.650
<i>I won't make it to the prelims,
 let alone nationals!</i>

00:04:21.520 --> 00:04:24.030
Could you please tutor me?!

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:30.040
I wish I could, but I'm 
not exactly a top student.

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:33.330
I'm in pretty hot water, too.

00:04:33.710 --> 00:04:36.460
So I plan to study with my boyfriend.

00:04:37.650 --> 00:04:39.210
You have a boyfriend?

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:42.120
An older man! We're still 
in the honeymoon phase.

00:04:42.560 --> 00:04:46.720
Maybe I'll hit him with the sad 
puppy eyes when I ask him for help!

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:47.470
You have a life...

00:04:47.690 --> 00:04:52.160
<i>That's right... I guess everyone's 
got their own studyin' to do...</i>

00:04:52.160 --> 00:04:54.750
<i>What now?!</i>

00:04:55.620 --> 00:04:59.110
I've been really looking 
forward to this interview!

00:04:59.110 --> 00:05:00.680
Thank you for coming!

00:05:00.680 --> 00:05:02.610
Thank you for having us.

00:05:02.610 --> 00:05:05.180
You're idols and full-time 
high school students.

00:05:05.180 --> 00:05:08.810
Readers your age are wildly curious

00:05:08.810 --> 00:05:10.370
about your school life.

00:05:11.440 --> 00:05:12.820
We're enjoying it.

00:05:12.820 --> 00:05:14.500
Every day is well spent.

00:05:14.910 --> 00:05:17.040
How are your grades?

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:20.390
<i>Oh, yeah! These guys are crazy busy, too.</i>

00:05:20.390 --> 00:05:22.000
<i>I bet they're havin' trouble.</i>

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:26.560
Well, I did get one of our grade's 
top three scores on our last midterms.

00:05:26.560 --> 00:05:27.180
<i>Huh?!</i>

00:05:27.180 --> 00:05:29.690
Really? I'm a little behind.

00:05:29.690 --> 00:05:32.140
I was in the top ten, though.

00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:33.670
<i>What's with these two?!</i>

00:05:33.670 --> 00:05:36.640
<i>They said they didn't care 
if they got expelled!</i>

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:39.560
Oh, wow. You're both great students!

00:05:39.560 --> 00:05:43.990
Whether it's career or school, my philosophy
 is to give my all to everything I do.

00:05:43.990 --> 00:05:48.660
Idols have to excel in multiple fields, 
to be worthy of being looked up to.

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:50.940
A failing grade wouldn't look good.

00:05:53.160 --> 00:05:54.960
Are we doing voice training next?

00:05:54.960 --> 00:05:57.770
Yeah, then a radio meeting.

00:05:59.260 --> 00:06:04.690
<i>"An 'action' is a discrete act, 
while an 'activity' is..."</i>

00:06:05.240 --> 00:06:07.030
Someone's slacking.

00:06:07.410 --> 00:06:08.800
Better cut her pay.

00:06:08.800 --> 00:06:10.710
I-I'm not slackin'!

00:06:10.710 --> 00:06:14.700
I got permission from Uchida-san 
to study during downtime!

00:06:14.700 --> 00:06:15.370
We know.

00:06:15.370 --> 00:06:16.810
We're just messing with you.

00:06:17.340 --> 00:06:22.060
Why are you suddenly studying, 
anyway? You never did before.

00:06:22.060 --> 00:06:25.570
Well, I'm dealing with
 some dire circumstances...

00:06:25.570 --> 00:06:28.500
You can't do sports with a failing grade.

00:06:28.500 --> 00:06:31.450
So if you don't do well on your finals, 
you can't compete this summer.

00:06:32.680 --> 00:06:33.970
He guessed right, eh?

00:06:34.400 --> 00:06:36.940
Um, can I ask you a favor?

00:06:36.940 --> 00:06:39.210
There are a lot of things 
I don't understand...

00:06:39.840 --> 00:06:42.670
Would you do me the great 
honor of tutoring me?!

00:06:42.670 --> 00:06:43.710
Excuse me?

00:06:47.280 --> 00:06:50.220
I'm sorry. Never mind.

00:06:54.940 --> 00:06:56.720
<i>I gotta try hard on my own,</i>

00:06:57.590 --> 00:06:59.550
<i>so that I can make my dream come true!</i>

00:07:02.040 --> 00:07:06.200
This will be on the test, 
so be sure to remember it.

00:07:02.860 --> 00:07:10.360
<b>Classics B</b>

00:07:06.790 --> 00:07:09.510
Next, another famous waka poem:

00:07:09.510 --> 00:07:12.340
"Spring, it seems, has passed, 
And the summer come again;

00:07:12.340 --> 00:07:15.090
For the silk-white robes, 
So 'tis said, are spread to dry

00:07:15.090 --> 00:07:16.420
On the 'Mount of Heaven's Perfume.'"

00:07:17.140 --> 00:07:21.120
This poem by Empress Jito is 
in the <i>Hyakunin Isshu</i>, as well.

00:07:21.120 --> 00:07:22.540
As a summer poem...

00:07:24.800 --> 00:07:25.780
Hello?

00:07:26.760 --> 00:07:30.320
Exams are coming up, so please do your 
best to fight off your sleepiness.

00:07:30.320 --> 00:07:31.380
Y-Yes, sir!

00:07:35.140 --> 00:07:41.640
<b>Classics B</b>

00:07:35.440 --> 00:07:37.040
As I was saying...

00:07:43.650 --> 00:07:45.900
<b>Yujiro</b>

00:07:43.650 --> 00:07:45.900
<b>Aizo</b>

00:07:46.640 --> 00:07:48.020
I got more.

00:07:48.020 --> 00:07:50.020
No, I got more.

00:07:50.020 --> 00:07:53.490
My total number of presents 
is clearly greater.

00:07:53.490 --> 00:07:55.530
Look how thick my stack of fan letters is.

00:07:55.530 --> 00:07:58.410
And my stack of presents is heavy as hell.

00:07:58.980 --> 00:08:00.160
That's enough!

00:08:00.470 --> 00:08:04.460
Gifts from fans aren't 
something to compete over.

00:08:05.040 --> 00:08:09.960
But aren't more and bigger obviously better?

00:08:09.960 --> 00:08:13.220
Size and volume are important, 
but weight is crucial, too.

00:08:13.440 --> 00:08:16.660
Size? Volume? Weight?

00:08:16.660 --> 00:08:18.750
Honestly, what do you take your fans for?

00:08:18.750 --> 00:08:20.920
The most important thing is their <i>feelings</i>.

00:08:23.020 --> 00:08:25.220
Goods that fans will like?

00:08:25.220 --> 00:08:28.340
I think we should hand out 
swag at your next event.

00:08:28.690 --> 00:08:31.240
And I'd like you two to think 
about what it should be.

00:08:31.520 --> 00:08:32.870
Why us?

00:08:32.870 --> 00:08:35.720
I don't know what girls like.

00:08:35.720 --> 00:08:38.910
Oh, dear. You aren't about to 
say something pathetic like,

00:08:38.910 --> 00:08:42.000
"I can't do what I don't 
understand," are you?

00:08:42.470 --> 00:08:46.930
The appeal will be that <i>you</i> 
suggested this for the fans.

00:08:46.930 --> 00:08:50.000
So sit down and really think 
about your fans' feelings.

00:08:50.760 --> 00:08:55.090
Other than that... Maybe a 
paper fan, or a message card?

00:08:55.090 --> 00:08:56.510
Too clichéd.

00:08:56.810 --> 00:08:59.440
An accessory, then? Like a hair tie.

00:08:59.440 --> 00:09:01.770
Not bad, but it lacks impact.

00:09:02.050 --> 00:09:05.520
Hey, come up with your own ideas 
instead of just dissing mine!

00:09:05.520 --> 00:09:09.020
I am thinking. Be quiet a minute.

00:09:09.590 --> 00:09:11.710
The fans' feelings...

00:09:16.450 --> 00:09:17.230
What?

00:09:17.630 --> 00:09:19.040
I need a change of scenery.

00:09:21.500 --> 00:09:23.500
Quit copying me!

00:09:23.500 --> 00:09:24.870
Quit copying <i>me</i>.

00:09:26.250 --> 00:09:30.460
<b>Japanese History</b>

00:09:30.460 --> 00:09:32.490
I title this sculpture "Hard Times."

00:09:32.490 --> 00:09:34.330
"Hard Fight" is better.

00:09:34.850 --> 00:09:38.010
I'm in a crisis here! I don't 
have time for your bullyin'!

00:09:38.260 --> 00:09:41.510
Okay, okay. We're busy, too.

00:09:41.510 --> 00:09:43.010
Enjoy your studying.

00:09:43.860 --> 00:09:48.990
"The <i>Shin Kokin Wakashu</i> was compiled 
in the early Kamakura Period.

00:09:48.990 --> 00:09:54.440
It is 20 volumes total. Fujiwara no Teika 
was one of the compilers selected."

00:09:54.440 --> 00:09:56.540
Why did you come to Tokyo?

00:09:56.540 --> 00:09:57.400
Huh?

00:09:58.050 --> 00:09:59.940
Were you recruited by a track scout?

00:10:00.300 --> 00:10:03.950
No, I'm not that great an athlete.

00:10:04.390 --> 00:10:08.540
I just happened to have a connection 
to the teacher who's my advisor now.

00:10:08.910 --> 00:10:11.880
He asked me if I wanted to 
keep runnin' at Sakuragaoka.

00:10:13.030 --> 00:10:14.920
But you could've run in your hometown, right?

00:10:14.920 --> 00:10:19.020
None of the nearby high 
schools have track teams.

00:10:19.360 --> 00:10:21.430
I told myself I had to give up...

00:10:22.480 --> 00:10:24.430
but I just couldn't.

00:10:25.190 --> 00:10:29.500
Then he invited me, so I knew I had to come!

00:10:29.940 --> 00:10:32.680
Because I love to run.

00:10:33.440 --> 00:10:34.870
Not exactly deep.

00:10:34.870 --> 00:10:36.450
That was the only reason?

00:10:38.330 --> 00:10:40.990
That and the support, I guess.

00:10:45.320 --> 00:10:50.500
When I race, my friends and 
family all cheer me on.

00:10:50.780 --> 00:10:53.000
They yell, "Go! You can do it!"

00:10:53.730 --> 00:10:57.520
If I finish first, they go wild.

00:10:57.520 --> 00:11:01.510
I was so happy to get a first-place medal.

00:11:02.230 --> 00:11:06.330
I went around showin' it to everyone 
and thankin' them for the support.

00:11:09.580 --> 00:11:12.020
You've got amazin' support too, huh?

00:11:12.020 --> 00:11:13.100
Huh?

00:11:13.100 --> 00:11:14.020
How so?

00:11:14.020 --> 00:11:16.540
I mean the fan letters and presents!

00:11:17.510 --> 00:11:21.910
I could tell just by lookin' at 
'em how much the senders cared.

00:11:21.910 --> 00:11:26.330
I could almost hear each 
one sayin', "You can do it!"

00:11:28.830 --> 00:11:33.080
With that many people supportin' ya, 
it's hard <i>not</i> to do your best, right?

00:11:33.740 --> 00:11:34.880
Support...

00:11:37.840 --> 00:11:39.140
Hmm? What's—

00:11:39.140 --> 00:11:41.390
Shouldn't you be studying?

00:11:41.390 --> 00:11:43.840
Shoot, I forgot!

00:11:43.840 --> 00:11:45.470
<b>Japanese History</b>

00:11:45.470 --> 00:11:45.600
<b>Japanese History</b>

00:11:45.600 --> 00:11:45.720
<b>Japanese History</b>

00:11:45.720 --> 00:11:45.870
<b>Japanese History</b>

00:11:45.750 --> 00:11:49.350
What'll I do? I'll never finish this!

00:11:49.350 --> 00:11:53.120
You don't have enough time for 
everything that might be on the test.

00:11:53.460 --> 00:11:54.860
Memorize just the main points.

00:11:55.230 --> 00:11:56.590
Main points...

00:11:58.410 --> 00:11:59.360
What are they?!

00:12:07.210 --> 00:12:09.030
These two parts.

00:12:09.030 --> 00:12:11.120
Give me your math book.

00:12:11.120 --> 00:12:13.410
I'll tell you which parts are 
guaranteed to be on the test,

00:12:13.410 --> 00:12:14.950
so master those parts.

00:12:15.620 --> 00:12:17.620
Then at least you won't fail.

00:12:19.120 --> 00:12:20.260
Why help me?

00:12:20.260 --> 00:12:21.840
I just felt like it.

00:12:21.840 --> 00:12:24.260
Hurry up before I change my mind.

00:12:27.320 --> 00:12:28.170
Okay!

00:12:35.060 --> 00:12:36.930
It's beautiful!

00:12:37.560 --> 00:12:39.640
Hello, Hiyoko.

00:12:39.640 --> 00:12:42.070
Hello, Uchida-san!

00:12:42.070 --> 00:12:43.730
Wait, where are they?

00:12:43.730 --> 00:12:45.840
They're filming in the woods.

00:12:45.840 --> 00:12:48.360
Sorry to bring you in on the 
first day off after exams.

00:12:48.360 --> 00:12:53.660
It's totally fine! I'm itchin' to move 
my body now that tests are over.

00:12:53.660 --> 00:12:54.960
I'm gonna work hard!

00:12:54.960 --> 00:12:56.960
That's a big help.

00:12:57.590 --> 00:13:00.460
This place is really something.

00:13:00.460 --> 00:13:02.150
It's a wedding venue.

00:13:02.150 --> 00:13:05.620
Why don't you get married here one day?

00:13:05.620 --> 00:13:07.420
What, me?!

00:13:09.870 --> 00:13:12.590
Nope, I can't imagine it.

00:13:12.590 --> 00:13:14.800
Oh? You don't dream about getting married?

00:13:14.800 --> 00:13:17.480
I've never liked someone that way.

00:13:18.300 --> 00:13:19.630
Hiyori-chan!

00:13:19.630 --> 00:13:21.020
We're unloading!

00:13:21.020 --> 00:13:22.980
G-Got it!

00:13:25.990 --> 00:13:28.990
And voilà—we have a ballroom!

00:13:28.990 --> 00:13:32.330
Wow! It's like a fairy tale setting!

00:13:33.020 --> 00:13:35.580
This is the "Nonfantasy" video, after all.

00:13:36.180 --> 00:13:37.760
Look, she's here.

00:13:37.760 --> 00:13:39.840
The fairy tale main character.

00:13:40.070 --> 00:13:42.590
Hello, everyone!

00:13:42.590 --> 00:13:47.520
Oh, she's cute! I think I've 
seen her before somewhere.

00:13:48.460 --> 00:13:53.640
That's Yumeru-san. She started as an 
amateur model, and she's popular lately.

00:13:53.640 --> 00:13:55.590
Apparently she's a huge LIP×LIP fan.

00:13:55.590 --> 00:13:56.850
Wow.

00:13:56.850 --> 00:13:59.480
<i>She's like a real-life princess!</i>

00:14:00.110 --> 00:14:02.240
Here, put this away.

00:14:02.660 --> 00:14:03.800
This, too.

00:14:04.780 --> 00:14:08.190
<i>Sheesh, I'm not a garment rack!</i>

00:14:08.890 --> 00:14:13.300
<i>They both look super princely, though!</i>

00:14:13.300 --> 00:14:15.290
How'd your tests go?

00:14:15.930 --> 00:14:17.750
I gave them my all!

00:14:17.750 --> 00:14:20.980
Effort doesn't matter if you don't get results.

00:14:20.980 --> 00:14:23.500
Hard work doesn't always pay off.

00:14:23.500 --> 00:14:28.680
Don't jinx me! It <i>will</i> pay 
off and I <i>will</i> get results!

00:14:34.320 --> 00:14:35.880
Hey, you.

00:14:35.880 --> 00:14:36.770
Yes?

00:14:37.280 --> 00:14:38.600
<i>It's the princess!</i>

00:14:38.960 --> 00:14:42.420
You're part of their staff, right? 
Are you friendly with them?

00:14:42.420 --> 00:14:43.180
Huh?

00:14:43.180 --> 00:14:44.800
What's your relationship?

00:14:44.800 --> 00:14:46.610
Well, I'm...

00:14:46.610 --> 00:14:49.740
The fact that you're in their class

00:14:49.740 --> 00:14:51.990
and the fact that you're their 
manager are both secrets.

00:14:52.280 --> 00:14:55.450
Rumors can kill an idol's career.

00:14:55.680 --> 00:14:59.900
Um, I work part-time at their agency.

00:14:59.900 --> 00:15:01.450
Hmm...

00:15:01.450 --> 00:15:04.340
Yumeru-chan! We're starting!

00:15:04.340 --> 00:15:05.750
Yes, sir!

00:15:09.480 --> 00:15:11.290
What was that about?

00:15:11.970 --> 00:15:17.060
<i>We'll be in love for decades, for centuries</i>

00:15:17.060 --> 00:15:22.480
<i>We'll always be drawn to 
each other, like magic</i>

00:15:38.020 --> 00:15:40.790
<i>A grand fairy tale world...</i>

00:15:41.550 --> 00:15:43.870
<i>Beautiful leading characters...</i>

00:15:44.190 --> 00:15:45.850
<i>In comparison...</i>

00:15:46.900 --> 00:15:50.710
<i>I'm just a nameless bit part.</i>

00:15:54.740 --> 00:15:57.310
Thirty-minute break, everyone!

00:16:05.750 --> 00:16:08.050
Great work today. Here you go.

00:16:08.050 --> 00:16:09.130
Thanks.

00:16:10.180 --> 00:16:11.590
Thank you.

00:16:14.720 --> 00:16:17.190
<i>It looks delicious.</i>

00:16:24.030 --> 00:16:25.080
Eat.

00:16:25.360 --> 00:16:29.090
Huh?! But I'm just an underling... I couldn't...

00:16:29.470 --> 00:16:31.450
No need to be shy.

00:16:31.450 --> 00:16:35.840
We wouldn't be able to film this video 
without all the hardworking staff.

00:16:36.920 --> 00:16:39.170
Well, don't mind if I do—

00:16:39.170 --> 00:16:39.850
You there.

00:16:40.320 --> 00:16:43.130
Could you bring the director some coffee?

00:16:43.130 --> 00:16:44.370
Oh, okay!

00:16:51.980 --> 00:16:53.360
How could you?!

00:16:53.990 --> 00:16:55.860
I-I'm so sorry.

00:16:55.860 --> 00:16:57.530
Don't touch me.

00:16:57.810 --> 00:17:01.040
It's just cruel to ruin my dress 
when the shoot isn't over yet!

00:17:02.510 --> 00:17:03.660
Are you all right?

00:17:04.150 --> 00:17:07.540
Excuse me! Towel, please!

00:17:10.700 --> 00:17:13.260
Are you all right? You're not burned?

00:17:13.770 --> 00:17:15.760
I apologize for our staff.

00:17:16.240 --> 00:17:18.050
I'm really sorry.

00:17:19.550 --> 00:17:21.880
It's not your fault.

00:17:22.200 --> 00:17:25.050
But what'll I do about this costume?

00:17:25.050 --> 00:17:26.810
Shall we go back to the green room?

00:17:26.810 --> 00:17:27.950
Yeah...

00:17:45.570 --> 00:17:47.100
Hey, you in there?

00:17:49.150 --> 00:17:50.340
Hello!

00:17:51.610 --> 00:17:54.650
I can't come to the phone right now.

00:17:54.650 --> 00:17:57.560
No dumb jokes, please.

00:17:57.560 --> 00:18:01.350
The shoot is over. If you don't 
come out, we'll leave you here.

00:18:03.030 --> 00:18:04.350
Please do.

00:18:04.840 --> 00:18:10.280
Why are you so depressed? 
You screwing up is nothing new.

00:18:10.280 --> 00:18:11.860
You do it all the time.

00:18:13.360 --> 00:18:15.440
This is different.

00:18:15.440 --> 00:18:17.490
Different how?

00:18:17.490 --> 00:18:22.370
I... caused you trouble.

00:18:23.160 --> 00:18:25.370
I made you apologize.

00:18:26.820 --> 00:18:27.930
I'm sorry.

00:18:30.620 --> 00:18:31.900
Excuse me.

00:18:33.880 --> 00:18:37.340
Aizo-kun, Yujiro-kun, thank you for today.

00:18:37.340 --> 00:18:41.700
No, thank you. But didn't 
we say our goodbyes already?

00:18:42.980 --> 00:18:46.930
Would you be willing to 
give me your phone numbers?

00:18:47.390 --> 00:18:51.560
I'm sorry, but that's 
against our agency's rules.

00:18:55.720 --> 00:18:57.740
But you're fine with her?

00:18:59.970 --> 00:19:02.970
You should watch out for girls like that.

00:19:02.970 --> 00:19:08.180
For all you know, she took a job 
at your agency to get close to you!

00:19:08.870 --> 00:19:10.750
That's <i>your</i> motive.

00:19:12.540 --> 00:19:14.470
This is the problem with women.

00:19:15.460 --> 00:19:18.760
Don't try to get up close and personal 
with us just because we co-starred.

00:19:19.760 --> 00:19:24.510
I saw you trip her, you know.

00:19:24.510 --> 00:19:28.570
Nonsense! I wouldn't do that! 
You must be mistaken—

00:19:28.570 --> 00:19:30.790
We can settle this by 
checking the camera footage.

00:19:30.790 --> 00:19:34.020
Not the crew's cameras. The security cameras.

00:19:35.270 --> 00:19:42.410
Don't you have the imagination to realize 
messing with our staff would annoy us?

00:19:43.350 --> 00:19:46.910
Your fake crying isn't bad, 
but I suggest you don't pursue acting.

00:19:47.470 --> 00:19:49.920
It's not a career for 
people who lack imagination.

00:19:53.990 --> 00:19:57.330
Watch it. You've totally 
dropped your game face.

00:19:57.330 --> 00:19:59.560
It's her fault for pissing me off.

00:19:59.560 --> 00:20:02.610
And you were openly picking a fight.

00:20:02.610 --> 00:20:05.750
She knows I know her weaknesses.

00:20:06.220 --> 00:20:09.730
And if she does decide to 
fight back, I'll destroy her career.

00:20:09.730 --> 00:20:11.100
Ooh, scary.

00:20:11.100 --> 00:20:15.650
You heard us. You didn't do anything 
wrong, so get out here already.

00:20:17.890 --> 00:20:22.570
Quit hesitating. It's out of 
character for you, Potato Face.

00:20:23.080 --> 00:20:25.070
Don't call me that!

00:20:25.340 --> 00:20:27.320
Here's the potato girl.

00:20:27.320 --> 00:20:28.580
Let's go home.

00:20:29.110 --> 00:20:33.910
I guess she'd be fine if we left, 
anyway. She could run home.

00:20:33.910 --> 00:20:36.330
Yeah, it'd be easy for her. 
She runs every day.

00:20:36.330 --> 00:20:38.840
What? No way! Wait for me!

00:20:40.210 --> 00:20:46.470
<i>It's strange... They're not in their costumes, 
but they still seem kinda princely.</i>

00:20:50.080 --> 00:20:50.950
Kikuchi.

00:20:51.560 --> 00:20:52.320
Here.

00:20:52.800 --> 00:20:53.600
Kudo.

00:20:54.100 --> 00:20:55.060
Here.

00:20:55.060 --> 00:20:55.930
Kodama.

00:20:56.330 --> 00:20:57.100
Here.

00:20:57.520 --> 00:20:58.610
Sakaue.

00:20:58.610 --> 00:20:59.560
Here.

00:21:00.160 --> 00:21:01.410
Shibasaki.

00:21:01.410 --> 00:21:02.090
Here.

00:21:02.630 --> 00:21:03.500
Suzumi.

00:21:04.640 --> 00:21:05.630
Suzumi!

00:21:05.630 --> 00:21:07.050
H-Here!

00:21:08.900 --> 00:21:12.300
<i>How'd I do, Sensei?</i>

00:21:12.300 --> 00:21:14.370
<i>Am I out? Safe?</i>

00:21:14.370 --> 00:21:17.880
<i>I can't tell what he's thinkin'!</i>

00:21:18.190 --> 00:21:19.530
Here you go.

00:21:19.530 --> 00:21:20.880
Th-Thank you.

00:21:24.830 --> 00:21:25.910
<i>Any failing grades?</i>

00:21:27.090 --> 00:21:28.070
<i>No!</i>

00:21:28.070 --> 00:21:29.640
Safe, eh?

00:21:30.590 --> 00:21:33.360
Hey, don't look without askin'!

00:21:33.360 --> 00:21:34.930
Just barely, though.

00:21:34.930 --> 00:21:39.150
Isn't that a success? 
"Just barely" lets her compete.

00:21:40.190 --> 00:21:41.560
That's great.

00:21:42.400 --> 00:21:44.110
Y-Yeah.

00:21:45.500 --> 00:21:49.230
<i>Idol smiles might be dangerous.</i>

00:21:51.030 --> 00:21:55.040
<b>Episode 3</b>

00:21:51.030 --> 00:21:55.040
<b>Nonfantasy</b>

00:23:26.400 --> 00:23:33.160
Next time, on episode 4 of 
<i>Heroines Run the Show</i>...

00:23:33.160 --> 00:23:35.050
"What I Can Do"!

00:23:33.990 --> 00:23:40.250
<b>Episode 4
What I Can Do</b>
